# --- environment ----------------------------------------------------------
# Root-only: a nested ".venv" belongs to another project and is not ours.
/.venv/

# Root-only: the unanchored "state/" matched a "state" directory at any depth.
# Keep nested state dirs (fixtures, sub-projects) visible to git.
/state/

# Root-only ON PURPOSE.  The unanchored rule "dockets/" also matched a
# directory named "dockets" at any depth - including the test fixture tree
# tests/fixtures/dashboard-store/dockets/**, whose ok-docket/broken-docket
# fixtures were therefore untracked and absent on a fresh clone.
# Whether produced dockets should be versioned at all is an open question for
# the user; anchoring preserves today's behaviour (root dockets stay ignored).
/dockets/

# --- generated databases --------------------------------------------------
# SQLite sidecars are runtime state, never source.  Global by design: any
# *.sqlite database can grow a -wal/-shm/-journal next to it.
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-journal
# The dashboard fixture DB is generated on demand into a session tmp_path by
# tests/fixtures/dashboard-store/build.py; a committed copy can silently
# disagree with the generator.
/tests/fixtures/dashboard-store/state.sqlite

# --- python build/cache output (genuinely global) -------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
# Root-only, like the venv above.
/.pytest_cache/

# --- temporary artifacts (global by design) ---------------------------------
# A *.tmp file is scratch at any depth: the kg-refresh lane's s.tmp under
# state/, editor scratch at the repo root, spill files in the source tree.
# The 4 existing state/**/s.tmp files were already ignored transitively by
# /state/ above; this rule additionally covers a root-level or src/ *.tmp that
# /state/ never reached (the gap U8.67's staging rehearsal found).
**/*.tmp
